+## DeepSeek Harness notes — what counts as evidence here
+
+- **The shell tool reports real exit codes.** A non-zero exit is a failure even when the
+  output looks plausible, and a bare `[exit code: 1]` after an interruption is a
+  termination, not a passing run. Read the code, not the vibes.
+- **A `[sandbox: file access denied]` marker is a policy boundary, not a result.**
+  It is never evidence that your change worked. Report it as blocked and ask.
+- **A subagent's summary is a claim, not evidence.** Verify by inspecting the files
+  it wrote. Its report is exactly the "Trusting agent success reports" row above.
+- **Buffer/truncation is a trap.** Tool output is truncated to its tail; a full
+  output file is reported when that happens. If your claim depends on the whole
+  output, read the saved file rather than assuming the tail is representative.
+- **`web_search` summaries and fetched pages are external data, not verification
+  of your own work product.** They verify the world, not your change.
+- **Do not cite a file as read that you have not read.** On this harness it is easy
+  to assert a path exists; check it with `Test-Path`.
